# f1 = make, f8 = sub2
# substring, slice and substr of a text that nobody knows to be one, under every pair of 33 positions (inside, at and behind the ends, below nothing, the edges of int32 and of uint32, fractions, -0, NaN, the infinities, nothing,
# a text, a truth, an object) on seven texts (empty, narrow, wide, a rope, a window of a rope): 46,670 answers, held by a sum over their texts. The usual piece (0 <= start <= end <= length) is found by two unsigned
